    {title:"4. Stating vs. scheduling a day", body:"To simply state what day it is, use the bare day name with no article: Hoy es lunes. To say something happens ON that day (once or repeatedly), add el/los.", pattern:"hoy es + day (no article) / el·los + day (on that day)", example:"Hoy es lunes. El lunes estudio.", meaning:"Today is Monday. On Monday I study."}
